# Env files (never commit secrets)
.env
=======
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Personal academic records — never commit
#
# Study plans and transcripts carry a student's name, ID, advisor, GPA and
# full grade history. Both the source PDFs and anything parsed out of them
# are personal data.
#
# These patterns are deliberately broad and path-independent: the previous
# rule was `data/extracted/*.json`, which matched only files sitting directly
# in that directory. A parsed plan written one level deeper would have been
# committed.
data/plans/*.pdf
data/transcripts/
*_plan_*.pdf
*_plan_*.json
*transcript*.pdf
*transcript*.json
!tests/**/*transcript*.json

# Course syllabi are NOT personal and stay tracked: data/syllabi/ holds the
# source PDFs and the parser tests use them as fixtures. The collection
# checklist derived from the plans (data/plans/required_syllabi.md) carries
# only course codes and names, so it stays tracked too.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated artifacts — rebuilt from tracked inputs
#
# Extraction output for real syllabi. Regenerate in ~25 min from the tracked
# PDFs with:  python -m careercompass.cli.extract_all_syllabi
data/extracted/syllabi/
data/extracted/skills/

# Job-corpus artifacts, all rebuilt by extract_job_skills. The term pool runs
# to tens of megabytes because it holds every term the corpus produced, not
# only those above the cutoff; the ontology is small but equally derived, and
# its consumers read it from PostgreSQL.
data/extracted/jobs/

# Taxonomy artifacts. custom_skills.json is a source file and stays tracked;
# these are rebuilt by run_taxonomy_build, and the ESCO crawl cache runs to
# tens of megabytes.
data/taxonomy/cache/
data/taxonomy/taxonomy.jsonl
data/taxonomy/vector_index.npz

# Scratch output
data/temp/

# data/mock/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It is generated, but regenerating it
# costs ~3.5 hours of local GPU time and requires Ollama, and it is what lets
# anyone else on the team build against M2/M3 before the real syllabi are
# collected. Every record carries "mock": true and a WARNING field, and nothing
# in the real pipeline reads it — see docs/ENGINEERING_NOTES.md §10.

# Planning notes
SKILL_EXTRACTION_PLAN.md

# Packaging
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Course catalog pulls. Cached so re-indexing needs no re-fetch, and
# git-ignored because this is the only place course descriptions live and
# they are not ours to redistribute — see docs/ENGINEERING_NOTES.md.
data/raw/catalog/
